<!-- PAGE 5 --><div class="page-wrapper" data-page="5"><div class="page sp-dark">
<div style="padding:20px 32px"><div class="sp-bg-title">BACKGROUND</div>
<div class="sp-bg-q">1. WHAT IS A SOIL CARBON PROJECT?</div><div class="sp-bg-card">Soil organic carbon (SOC) is the carbon stored in organic matter in your soil. When you improve how you manage your land through better grazing, fertiliser use, or pasture practice you build more carbon in the ground. The Australian Government (Clean Energy Regulator) assesses that increase and issues carbon credits to you in the form of Australian Carbon Credit Units (ACCUs).</div>
<div class="sp-bg-q">2. WHAT IS AN ACCU?</div><div class="sp-bg-card">An ACCU (Australian Carbon Credit Unit) is a government-backed carbon credit issued by the Clean Energy Regulator (CER). Each ACCU represents one tonne of CO₂ equivalent that has been stored in the soil or prevented from entering the atmosphere. ACCUs are a tradeable commodity. You can sell them to corporations, government programs, or hold them for future use.</div>
<div class="sp-bg-q">3. WHAT DOES IT MEAN FOR YOUR FARM?</div>
<div class="sp-bg-grid"><div class="sp-bg-benefit"><h4>Healthier Soil</h4><p>Higher soil carbon improves water-holding capacity and microbial activity. Your soil becomes more fertile and resilient over time.</p></div><div class="sp-bg-benefit"><h4>Drought Resilience</h4><p>Soils with higher carbon recover faster after dry periods and continue to perform in low-rainfall years.</p></div><div class="sp-bg-benefit"><h4>Greater Productivity</h4><p>Land with more soil carbon produces faster pasture growth and higher crop yields.</p></div><div class="sp-bg-benefit"><h4>New Income Stream</h4><p>ACCUs are issued to you as a landowner. You are earning an additional income stream from the management practices you intend to improve.</p></div></div>
</div></div></div>

